  "question": {
    "text": "Let the first term a and the common ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> of a geometric progression be positive integers. If the sum of squares of its first three terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33033</mn></math>, then the sum of these three terms is equal to",
